# {{ if .DisplayName }}{{ .DisplayName }}{{ else }}{{ .Container }}{{ end }}

The `{{ .Container }}` function of {{ .SoftwareSystem }}, in project {{ .Project }}: an AWS
Lambda function in Python (boto3) behind an API Gateway HTTP API, keeping
items in a DynamoDB table, with its infrastructure as a CDK app in
TypeScript. Scaffolded by C4 Factory.

## The API

Every request is signed with AWS credentials (SigV4): the API's routes use IAM
authorization, and a caller needs `execute-api:Invoke` on them.

| Route             | Body                                | Answers                                    |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| `PUT /items/{id}` | `{ "name": "Lamp", "quantity": 3 }` | 200 and the item; 400 for a bad id or body |
| `GET /items/{id}` |                                     | 200 and the item; 404 when there is none   |

An id is 1 to 64 letters, digits, `-` or `_`. A name is 1 to 200 characters;
a quantity a whole number from 0 to 2⁵³ − 1. Every error is JSON with a `message`.
A `PUT` replaces the whole item, so repeating it is harmless.

## Develop

Open the repository in its devcontainer, which has Node 24, uv and the Go
toolchain.

```sh
uv sync --locked # install the exact Python packages in uv.lock
npm ci           # install the exact CDK packages in package-lock.json
uv run pytest    # the function's tests
npm test         # the stacks' assertions, with vitest
npm run synth    # write the CloudFormation templates into cdk.out/
{{- if .Standard }}
make check       # what CI runs: format, lint, type check, test, synth, cfn-lint
make help        # every target
{{- end }}
```

Nothing here deploys or needs an AWS account: synth needs neither Docker nor
credentials. It bundles the function with uv: the packages `uv.lock` pins, as
wheels for arm64 Linux, from uv's cache or, for a wheel the cache lacks, PyPI. Deploying the stack (`cdk deploy`, after
`cdk bootstrap` of the account) is for its owner, with their own credentials.

## Layout

- `app/handler.py` is the Lambda entry point (`app.handler.handler`): it
  creates the DynamoDB table resource once, at module scope, reads
  `TABLE_NAME` and hands each request to `answer` in `app/api.py`.
- `app/api.py` routes a request, checks its input and answers with a status
  code; `app/items.py` holds the rules, free of AWS; `app/item_store.py`
  keeps items in DynamoDB behind the `ItemStore` protocol tests fake.
- `tests/` holds the function's pytest tests; none calls AWS.
- `infra/stacks.ts` defines the stacks; `infra/api_stack.ts` is the one
  stack: the table, the function with its log group and role, and the API
  with its access log. The stack is named after the package in
  `package.json`.
{{- if .Standard }}
- `infra/main.ts` is the CDK app `cdk synth` runs (`cdk.json`), and
  `infra/standard.ts` tags every stack and adds CDK Nag's checks.

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing anything: it is the rulebook, for people and agents.
{{- end }}
